<node id="11126143" title="Re: Calling module function from within a blessed module" created="2021-01-02 10:40:08" updated="2021-01-02 10:40:08" _doctext_mode="strict"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="830549">haukex</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;p&gt;Since both &lt;c&gt;do_something&lt;/c&gt; and &lt;c&gt;do_more&lt;/c&gt; appear to be methods, since they both take &lt;c&gt;$self&lt;/c&gt; as their first argument, then you probably should always call them as such.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;c&gt;
sub do_more {
    my $self = shift;
    return $self-&gt;do_something('example');
}
&lt;/c&gt;
</doctext>
